{
 "_createdAt": "2026-04-27T19:20:38Z",
 "_id": "wp-post-134632-en",
 "_rev": "S0nWQbQfCu6sjLYYx5pLN3",
 "_type": "article",
 "_updatedAt": "2026-11-09T18:01:04Z",
 "author": {
  "_ref": "author-legacy-archive",
  "_type": "reference"
 },
 "body": [
  {
   "_key": "000000000001",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000000",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "August Egypt travel isn't for everyone."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000003",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "9013tqorh5jf",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "The heat is real. In Upper Egypt — "
    },
    {
     "_key": "6v4dsbaw4lst",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "zaqkv1pk39pg"
     ],
     "text": "Luxor"
    },
    {
     "_key": "5l455dppa8l7",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", "
    },
    {
     "_key": "87csierrvto6",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "shqjzmtlgr0o"
     ],
     "text": "Aswan"
    },
    {
     "_key": "ifbkujz4xrr0",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", "
    },
    {
     "_key": "qjsujvqbgihm",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "sqi77y637imm"
     ],
     "text": "Abu Simbel"
    },
    {
     "_key": "t472ctet12xe",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " — daytime outdoor sightseeing turns quite harsh. Sun strong, sites short on shade, pushing afternoon drains overall trip stamina."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "zaqkv1pk39pg",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "shqjzmtlgr0o",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "sqi77y637imm",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-56813",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000005",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000004",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "August isn't completely unsuited. Less crowded, with hotels and tours easier than winter; on the Red Sea, sea travel works well. What matters is not carrying winter's itinerary as is."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000007",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000006",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "August Egypt isn't a trip against heat — it is a trip built to heat."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000009",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000008",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Split heat by region"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000000b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000000a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Egypt is wide; August feels differ greatly by region."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000000d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "h32tg0rm0stt",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "8dtkszs8m83l"
     ],
     "text": "Cairo"
    },
    {
     "_key": "ixhy40nbrsr5",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " and "
    },
    {
     "_key": "qmmshkhbh1p9",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "vytrwpxc7rwe"
     ],
     "text": "Giza"
    },
    {
     "_key": "nq7nhactx3hf",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " are hot but not as extreme as Luxor or Aswan. Outdoor pyramid plateau is morning-based; combined with GEM or indoor facilities, you can spend hot hours avoiding."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "8dtkszs8m83l",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "vytrwpxc7rwe",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000000f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "k5yd9y5s8shw",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Luxor and Aswan are the most carefully considered. "
    },
    {
     "_key": "zm534396n1m3",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "vkmhx98ctnfb"
     ],
     "text": "Valley of the Kings"
    },
    {
     "_key": "hrm4bl7o37rh",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", Karnak, Hatshepsut, Philae must be toured early morning. Late morning into afternoon, switch from outdoor to rest or indoor."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "vkmhx98ctnfb",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-kings",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000011",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "bnq9q3a7vmn6",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Red Sea coast is comparatively workable in August. "
    },
    {
     "_key": "7hv2096u6y8c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "h63omu97vch5"
     ],
     "text": "Hurghada"
    },
    {
     "_key": "ggmuibdwap02",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", Sharm el-Sheikh, "
    },
    {
     "_key": "hi83sa6be0hg",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "46iaehvej4ku"
     ],
     "text": "Marsa Alam"
    },
    {
     "_key": "m7oybvdjcc1w",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " have heat; sea, pool, and resort facilities centre the trip. Snorkelling and diving fit if scheduled to mornings and good sea conditions."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "h63omu97vch5",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58859",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "46iaehvej4ku",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58885",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000013",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "phjrkjlf48ig",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "lnkvup594gyu"
     ],
     "text": "Alexandria"
    },
    {
     "_key": "1n0rx4obu7k3",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " and Mediterranean coast can feel easier than inland. Humid but sea breeze gives a different summer city air from Cairo and Upper Egypt."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "lnkvup594gyu",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58750",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000015",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "f5cqbgbg2qwp",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Western Desert and "
    },
    {
     "_key": "l1cd7cy1zrqu",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "jsdwqpq9ic7e"
     ],
     "text": "Siwa Oasis"
    },
    {
     "_key": "cwbxbe5kumsy",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " get quite hot in August. Springs and salt lakes appeal; with long transfer, desert activity needs strict time selection. For first short trips, sometimes not forcing them in is wiser."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "jsdwqpq9ic7e",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58932",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000017",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000016",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Itineraries suited to August"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000019",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000018",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Most workable in August is a Cairo and Red Sea–centred trip."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000001b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000001a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Cairo see Giza pyramids, GEM, parts of Islamic Cairo; then Hurghada or Sharm el-Sheikh for sea time. Combines comparatively well with heat."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000001d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "2wnnjn2pvn23",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For serious ancient sites, including Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan works. Avoid winter-style all-day outdoor schedules. In Luxor — early-morning Valley of the Kings, late-morning one temple, midday hotel rest, evening "
    },
    {
     "_key": "lvywp3atwx09",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "0nr175u2zl2w"
     ],
     "text": "Luxor Temple"
    },
    {
     "_key": "iopwhcg2x5il",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " or felucca — that rhythm fits."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "0nr175u2zl2w",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.the-luxor-temple",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000001f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000001e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Placing Red Sea at the end eases the whole trip. After walking Cairo and Luxor, two or three days seaside leaves less pre-departure fatigue."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000021",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000020",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Conversely, packing Cairo, Luxor, Aswan, Abu Simbel, Red Sea, and desert in a short period gets heavy in August. Don't underestimate distance and heat together."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000023",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000022",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Day building"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000025",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000024",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In August trips, time use matters most."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000027",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000026",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Outdoor sites concentrate in the morning. Leave as early as possible; finish main viewing before heat strengthens. After midday — hotel, pool, air-conditioned museum, transfer, nap. Evening, head out again."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000029",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000028",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Just maintaining this simple rhythm greatly changes trip comfort."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000002b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "z009m4vk9dij",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Cairo — morning Giza, midday GEM or hotel, evening "
    },
    {
     "_key": "4ium5995hy6t",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "7erbkmlq963e"
     ],
     "text": "Khan el-Khalili"
    },
    {
     "_key": "3584onfn7fc0",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " or Nile-side. Luxor — early morning west bank, midday rest, evening Luxor Temple or Nile. Aswan — morning Philae, midday Nubian Museum or hotel, evening river time."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "7erbkmlq963e",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.cairo.khan-el-khalili",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000002d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000002c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Matching heat isn't giving up the trip. It is the base for using August Egypt well."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000002f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000002e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Cairo and Giza"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000031",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000030",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In August Cairo, combining outdoor and indoor is key."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000033",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000032",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Visit Giza pyramids early morning. The plateau has little shade and stone-sand reflection; late times drain. With camels or carriages, avoid hot times and confirm price and content in advance."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000035",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000034",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "GEM matters especially in August Cairo. Time indoors with Tutankhamun displays and ancient-Egyptian large flow makes it easy to build into hot-season itineraries. Hours and ticket conditions change; confirm official information."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000037",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000036",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Islamic Cairo and Khan el-Khalili walk more comfortably evening onward. Even with daytime heat remaining, light softens and city movement becomes more visible."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000039",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000038",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Luxor"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000003b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000003a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "August Luxor isn't unreachable. Strong discipline needed."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000003d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000003c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Valley of the Kings — early morning. Tomb interiors can feel cooler than outside; the valley itself sharpens once sun rises. Don't add too many tombs; narrow to what you want."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000003f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "atjj2l96288p",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Karnak, Hatshepsut, "
    },
    {
     "_key": "gke7gz6xvx24",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "k7gook8o1pyh"
     ],
     "text": "Medinet Habu"
    },
    {
     "_key": "38mee9vtt2my",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " also morning. All have impact; shade is limited. In August, time-of-day selection matters more than sight count."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "k7gook8o1pyh",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.madinat-habu-temple",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000041",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000040",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Evening Luxor Temple is comparatively workable in August. The temple lit after sunset has atmosphere, an experience different from daytime outdoor."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000043",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000042",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Luxor, hotel choice also matters. Stable cooling, rooms to rest in at midday, pool or shaded rest space — in August, not luxury but practical."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000045",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000044",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Aswan and Abu Simbel"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000047",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "okr9ro5514iw",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Aswan is beautiful; August is quite hot. Combining Philae, Unfinished Obelisk, "
    },
    {
     "_key": "73tn8agdktaj",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "vsb2dmxps4bz"
     ],
     "text": "Aswan High Dam"
    },
    {
     "_key": "smbzfgd90irp",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", and Nubian Museum — push outdoor to morning."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "vsb2dmxps4bz",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-59236",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000049",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "mi5yuy6huxdm",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Indoor facilities like "
    },
    {
     "_key": "yv3xgecn280z",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "by10uc772ek7"
     ],
     "text": "the Nubian Museum"
    },
    {
     "_key": "1dg4kftme0zg",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " suit midday. Aswan's Nile scenery and island time also appeal; don't fill all with sites — leave evening riverside."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "by10uc772ek7",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.aswan.the-nubian-museum",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000004b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000004a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Abu Simbel can be visited in August; consider both transfer and heat. Often long early-morning departure with strong sun on-site. With stamina concerns or children, easing the Aswan stay over forcing it in is also a choice."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000004d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000004c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "If including Abu Simbel, don't pack other plans that day."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000004f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000004e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Red Sea"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000051",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000050",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "One area working most naturally in August Egypt is the Red Sea."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000053",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000052",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Hurghada, Sharm el-Sheikh, Marsa Alam, entering the sea centres the trip. Snorkelling, diving, boat trips, pool, and resort rest are main ways to spend."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000055",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000054",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Sea doesn't mean safe. Sun is strong; on boats, burns easier. Hat, rash guard, sunscreen, hydration needed. At coral reefs, don't touch, don't stand, don't chase fish."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000057",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000056",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For diving, choose spots matching experience. Red Sea has beginner-calm places and current-prone advanced. Don't choose operators by price alone; confirm safety briefing, equipment, and guide ratio."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000059",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000058",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "If including Red Sea in August, placing at the trip's end fits. Resting after sightseeing fatigue, seeing another face of Egypt."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000005b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000005a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Alexandria"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000005d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000005c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Alexandria is easy to consider in August. Mediterranean coast; temperature can be more held than inland. As a summer seaside city, atmosphere different from Cairo or Luxor."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000005f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000005e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "August Alexandria crowds with Egyptian domestic travellers. Beach, Corniche, restaurants can be busy. Less quiet ruins and more feeling Egyptian summer city life."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000061",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "lz9iz8ig19cp",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Combining Citadel of Qaitbay, catacombs, Roman theatre, and "
    },
    {
     "_key": "9ewwj5cvrw33",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "t2ld8q16ylo3"
     ],
     "text": "Bibliotheca Alexandrina"
    },
    {
     "_key": "b62jq1c99blg",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " worth one night or day trip from Cairo. Short first trips can drop priority; itineraries avoiding heat sometimes fit."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "t2ld8q16ylo3",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.alexandria.bibliotheca-alexandrina",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000063",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000062",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Dress and gear"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000065",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000064",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In August Egypt, prioritise function over appearance."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000067",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000066",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Light breathable long sleeves, bright colours, walking shoes, brimmed hat, sunglasses. Showing skin isn't always cooler; clothing protecting from direct sun is sometimes easier."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000069",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000068",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For religious sites, covering shoulders and knees appropriate. Women — light scarf helps at mosques or churches."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000006b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000006a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Always carry water. Buy before outdoor visits, keep spare in the car. Oral rehydration, stomach medicine, after-sun care, and regular medication ready."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000006d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000006c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Sunscreen — premise reapplication. For Red Sea swimming, choose low-environmental-impact, and use physical sun blocks like rash guards."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000006f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000006e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Hotel choice"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000071",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000070",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In August, hotel choice ties directly to trip comfort."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000073",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000072",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Stable cooling. Location where return for midday rest works. Pool or shaded rest space. Early breakfast usable. Car and guide arrangement easy."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000075",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000074",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Luxor and Aswan especially, premise midday hotel return — room comfort matters. Early out, midday return, evening out again. Choose hotels fitting this rhythm."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000077",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000076",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "On Red Sea, confirm sea access. Sandy beach or jetty to reef? Easy for children to swim? Snorkel-suited house reef? Beyond name or stars, choose by how the sea is used to fail less."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000079",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000078",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Small inns and desert lodges may reduce summer operation. Before booking, directly confirm operating status, cooling, food, and transfer."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000007b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000007a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Food and condition"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000007d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000007c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In August, slight meal-time adjustment eases things."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000007f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000007e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Eat properly in the morning; avoid heavy food during outdoor sightseeing. Midday — light in air-conditioned places or hotel; evening — proper meal. The rhythm fits."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000081",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000080",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Premise tap water not being drunk. Bottled water; weak stomachs — care with ice and raw vegetables. With stamina dropping from heat, even usual meals can feel a load."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000083",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000082",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Watch dehydration signs. Headache, dullness, dizziness, dark urine, sweat suddenly stopping. With these states, prioritise rest over continuing."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000085",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000084",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Most important in August travel — protect condition, not schedule."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000087",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000086",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Itineraries to avoid in August"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000089",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000088",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Avoid in August — itineraries packing outdoor sites at midday."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000008b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000008a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Morning Giza, midday long Islamic Cairo walking, evening transfer. Next morning Luxor Valley of the Kings, midday Hatshepsut, afternoon Karnak. Such builds work on the map; physically quite harsh."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000008d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000008c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Also watch short-period itineraries including desert, Upper Egypt, and Red Sea all. Transfer days increase; transfer and waiting in hot hours overlap, losing margin to enjoy sightseeing itself."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000008f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000008e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "August needs courage to reduce numbers. Narrow destinations, choose times, build midday rest into plans. That ends up showing the most."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000091",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000090",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Is August worth going"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000093",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000092",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "August Egypt has clear advantages. Sites emptier than winter. Comparatively easier-to-get hotels. Warm Red Sea. Quiet morning Valley of the Kings. Evening Nile."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000095",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000094",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "The advantages premise heat handling. Take heat lightly and the trip suffers. Move with heat and August's quietness and margin appear."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000097",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000096",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For first Egypt travel with free season choice, October to April is easier. For weighing Luxor and Aswan especially, winter through early spring is natural."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000099",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000098",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For people only free in August, weighing Red Sea, avoiding crowds, or not minding early action, August Egypt holds. August Egypt isn't an easy season. Built right, not a bad season either. Needed — plans not pushing and a trip attitude valuing mornings."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  }
